# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Secrets -- but .env.example is the template the README tells you to copy
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Harbor local job output. The bundles are ignored; `jobs/` itself is NOT, for
# the same reason `sweep/_seed_*.json` is not -- see below. Those runs are paid
# LLM rollouts against the shipped tasks. They cost real money, they cannot be
# reproduced, and they are the only record of what a `harbor run` actually did.
# The tarballs they arrived in are regenerable from the logs; the logs are not
# regenerable from anything.
*.tar.gz

# Render/build intermediates. output/ is NOT ignored: output/pdf holds the
# compiled report, committed so a reader does not need a XeLaTeX + ctex install
# to read the deliverable. Rebuild with scripts/build_report.sh.
tmp/

# Eval sweep intermediates (regenerable via scripts; job logs are large)
sweep/instances/
sweep/runs/

# sweep/_seed_*.json is NOT ignored, and the reasoning that ignored it is worth
# keeping. They look like intermediates -- underscore-prefixed, off the
# `appworld_*.json` evidence convention, "regenerable via scripts" like
# everything above. They are not. Every other file in sweep/ comes from a
# deterministic probe: `appworld_donothing.json` re-emits byte-identically on
# demand. These are LLM rollouts. They cost real money, they cannot be
# reproduced, and they are the only evidence that any yield here was measured
# rather than observed. Classified by filename convention, they were one
# `git clean -xdf` from gone.

# AppWorld dataset (183M, re-fetch with: appworld download data)
appworld_data/

# `experiments/` used to be ignored on this line, sharing the AppWorld dataset's
# comment as though it were more re-fetchable bulk. It is not: it holds the probe
# outputs those measurements were read off, and nothing re-fetches it.

# Gaia2 mini split (162M parquet + unpacked scenarios; re-fetch with:
# uv run --with pandas --with pyarrow python -m scripts.gaia2_fetch)
gaia2_data/

# symlink to appworld_data (appworld expects ./data under APPWORLD_ROOT)
data

# Agent scratch. `.claude/worktrees/` holds isolated checkouts used while a
# long edit runs against a file the campaign is also writing; `.superpowers/`
# holds a plan's ledger, briefs, and review packages. Both are working state
# for a single session -- the commits they produce are the record, not these.
.claude/worktrees/
.superpowers/
